# 🔧 Development Workflow

## 📝 Commit Strategy

### Conventional Commits Format
```
type(scope): description

feat(booking): add Trafft integration with deposit handling
fix(i18n): correct Latvian translation keys for services  
chore(deps): update Next.js to latest stable version
docs(readme): add local development setup instructions
```

### Commit Types
- **feat**: New features or enhancements
- **fix**: Bug fixes and corrections
- **chore**: Maintenance, deps, config changes
- **docs**: Documentation updates
- **style**: Code formatting, no logic changes
- **refactor**: Code restructuring without behavior change
- **perf**: Performance improvements
- **test**: Test additions or modifications

### Scope Examples
- `booking`, `i18n`, `ui`, `forms`, `seo`, `api`, `styles`, `deps`

### Commit Rules
- Keep first line under 72 characters
- Use imperative mood ("add" not "added")
- Reference issues: `fixes #123` or `closes #456`
- Break large changes into logical commits
- Never commit broken code to main branch

## 🔍 PR Review Checklist

### Code Quality
- [ ] Follows TypeScript strict mode requirements
- [ ] Uses proper error handling with try/catch
- [ ] No console.log statements in production code
- [ ] Proper loading and error states for async operations
- [ ] Components are properly typed with interfaces

### Design System Compliance
- [ ] Uses shadcn/ui components before creating custom ones
- [ ] Follows Tailwind token system (no hard-coded values)
- [ ] Maintains spacing rhythm (24px/32px/40px)
- [ ] Typography follows serif/sans hierarchy
- [ ] Colors use brand tokens exclusively

### Accessibility
- [ ] Interactive elements are keyboard accessible
- [ ] Proper ARIA labels on buttons and form fields
- [ ] Semantic HTML structure maintained
- [ ] Color contrast meets WCAG AA standards
- [ ] Focus indicators visible and consistent

### Performance
- [ ] Images optimized and use Next.js Image component
- [ ] No unnecessary re-renders or effect loops
- [ ] Lazy loading implemented where appropriate
- [ ] Bundle size impact considered for new dependencies

### Testing
- [ ] Page loads without console errors
- [ ] Mobile responsiveness verified
- [ ] Cross-browser compatibility checked
- [ ] Internationalization tested (LV/RU/EN)

## 🌐 Internationalization Rules

### Translation Keys
```javascript
// ✅ Nested structure
t('nav.booking')          // "Rezervācija"
t('services.lashes.title') // "Skropstu pagarināšana"
t('form.validation.required') // "Šis lauks ir obligāts"

// ❌ Flat structure  
t('booking-nav-link')     // Avoid
t('lashes-service-title') // Avoid
```

### Key Naming Convention
- **Domain.component.element**: `booking.form.submit`
- **Domain.collection.item**: `services.lashes.classic`
- **Common.category.type**: `ui.buttons.primary`

### Translation Best Practices
- Always use `useTranslations()` hook for text
- Never hard-code strings in components
- Keep translation keys descriptive and hierarchical
- Include context in key names when meaning could be ambiguous
- Test all languages before merging

### Locale-Specific Considerations
- **Latvian**: Default locale, no URL prefix needed
- **Russian**: Cyrillic support, longer text considerations
- **English**: Fallback for missing translations
- **RTL**: Not needed for these languages
- **Pluralization**: Use next-intl plural forms when needed

## 🔍 SEO/Meta Conventions

### Page Metadata Template
```typescript
export const metadata: Metadata = {
  title: 'Page Title - Lash Bloom Studio',
  description: 'Concise description under 160 characters that includes key terms.',
  openGraph: {
    title: 'Page Title',
    description: 'Same or enhanced description for social sharing.',
    images: ['/og-images/page-specific.jpg'],
  },
};
```

### SEO Rules
- **Title**: Include page name + brand, under 60 characters
- **Description**: 140-160 characters, include target keywords naturally
- **H1**: One per page, matches title intent
- **Headings**: Logical hierarchy (H1→H2→H3), no levels skipped
- **URLs**: Clean, descriptive slugs in Latvian (primary language)

### JSON-LD Structured Data
```javascript
// For service pages
{
  "@type": "Service",
  "name": "Klasiskās skropstas", 
  "provider": "Lash Bloom Studio",
  "offers": {
    "price": "45",
    "priceCurrency": "EUR"
  }
}

// For business info
{
  "@type": "LocalBusiness",
  "name": "Lash Bloom Studio",
  "address": "Brīvības iela 123, Rīga"
}
```

## 📊 Analytics Hooks

### Event Tracking Strategy
```javascript
// Booking funnel
gtag('event', 'booking_step_1', { service_type: 'classic-lashes' });
gtag('event', 'booking_step_2', { master_selected: 'anna' });
gtag('event', 'booking_completed', { value: 45, currency: 'EUR' });

// Content engagement  
gtag('event', 'service_viewed', { service_id: 'volume-lashes' });
gtag('event', 'gallery_interaction', { image_index: 3 });
```

### Key Events to Track
- **Booking Flow**: Each step completion + abandonment points
- **Service Interest**: Which services get most views/clicks
- **Contact Attempts**: Phone clicks, form submissions
- **Language Switching**: Locale preferences and usage
- **Page Performance**: Core Web Vitals, error rates

### Privacy Compliance
- Cookie consent before analytics activation
- No PII in event parameters
- Respect Do Not Track headers
- GDPR-compliant data retention policies

## ⚡ Performance Tips

### Core Web Vitals Optimization
- **LCP**: Optimize hero images, preload critical fonts
- **FID**: Minimize JavaScript execution, use code splitting
- **CLS**: Specify image dimensions, avoid dynamic content injection

### Next.js Specific
```javascript
// Image optimization
<Image
  src="/hero-image.jpg"
  alt="Description"
  width={1200} height={800}
  priority={true} // For above-fold images
  placeholder="blur" // For better UX
/>

// Font optimization
const inter = Inter({ 
  subsets: ['latin'],
  display: 'swap', // Prevent FOIT
  variable: '--font-sans'
});

// Dynamic imports for code splitting
const BookingWidget = dynamic(() => import('./BookingWidget'), {
  loading: () => <BookingSkeleton />
});
```

### Bundle Optimization
- Audit bundle size with `npm run build`
- Use dynamic imports for large components
- Optimize third-party scripts (defer, async)
- Minimize polyfills for modern browsers

### Runtime Performance
- Use React.memo for expensive components
- Implement proper loading states
- Debounce search and form inputs
- Optimize re-renders with useMemo/useCallback

